{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"rounded-etymologic-karakul","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOn the AGENTIC path the growing tool-result history is re-sent UNCACHED every turn, so input cost\ngrows O(N^2) in turns — and rebar's own telemetry cannot see it.\n\n`capabilities.py:333-355` `cache_settings_for` sets exactly two of the four available breakpoints:\n\n    anthropic_cache_instructions=True\n    anthropic_cache_tool_definitions=True\n\nand its docstring says so outright: \"neither `*_cache_messages` nor `anthropic_cache` is touched.\"\nApplied once at `runner.py:394`.\n\nBOTH UNUSED KNOBS ALREADY EXIST in the pinned dependency — verified by introspection against the\nrepo's own `.venv` at pydantic-ai 1.107.1, not from docs:\n\n    AnthropicModelSettings: anthropic_cache, anthropic_cache_instructions,\n                            anthropic_cache_messages, anthropic_cache_tool_definitions\n    BedrockModelSettings:   bedrock_cache_instructions, bedrock_cache_messages,\n                            bedrock_cache_tool_definitions\n\n## The failure, concretely\n\n`DEFAULT_MAX_ITERATIONS = 250` (`config.py:127`) yields `request_limit = 125`\n(`structured_run.py:331`). The agentic Pass-1 criteria and container calls\n(`plan_review/passes.py:330, 434`) run a tool loop in which EVERY turn re-sends the full accumulated\nmessage history. With only a system breakpoint that history is never written to cache and never read.\nOn a 40-turn review whose file-read tool results average 2k tokens, turn 40 re-sends ~80k uncached\ntokens that turn 39 also sent.\n\nIT IS INVISIBLE TO OUR TELEMETRY. `warn_if_cache_ineffective` (`structured_run.py:417-422`) requires\n`cache_read_tokens == 0`, but the SYSTEM block IS hitting cache, so the counter is nonzero and the\npredicate never fires. We would never learn this from a usage log.\n\n## Consensus — this is the documented multi-turn shape, not an exotic optimisation\n\n* Anthropic's prompt-caching doc recommends TWO breakpoints for multi-turn: system AND \"the final\n  block of the final message... so the conversation can be incrementally cached\", and names automatic\n  caching the \"recommended starting point\" for multi-turn.\n* LangChain's `AnthropicPromptCachingMiddleware`\n  (`libs/partners/anthropic/langchain_anthropic/middleware/prompt_caching.py`) tags system + last tool\n  and delegates the tail to `model_settings[\"cache_control\"]`.\n* pydantic-ai's own Anthropic docs recommend the same triple.\nSystem-only is the documented minimum for a STATIC-PROMPT workload; it is not the shape for an agent.\n\nCorroborating that this was once in scope and got dropped: story REB-458 is titled \"Prompt caching at\nthe shared runner seam (CachePoint + anthropic_cache_*, provider-safe)\" and is marked Done, but the\nshipped `cache_settings_for` sets two of four knobs and no CachePoint.\n\n## Approach\n\nThread the execution mode into `cache_settings_for` and, for `agentic` ONLY, add\n`anthropic_cache=True` on the Anthropic arm and `bedrock_cache_messages=True` on the Bedrock arm.\n\nMIND THE PROVIDER ASYMMETRY — this is the trap: Bedrock has NO `bedrock_cache` automatic key. LangChain\nhit exactly this (langchain#37042): `AnthropicPromptCachingMiddleware` regressed on Bedrock in 1.4.1\nbecause it switched to top-level automatic caching, which Bedrock rejects with\n`cache_control: Extra inputs are not permitted`. So the two arms need different keys, not one shared\nsetting.\n\nBreakpoint budget is safe: pydantic-ai's `_limit_cache_points()` sets\n`MAX_CACHE_POINTS = 3 if automatic_caching else 4`, and this change puts rebar at 3.\n\nSingle-turn paths must stay BYTE-IDENTICAL — that is the regression risk and the thing to pin.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] On the AGENTIC path the message tail is cached: a captured multi-turn request shows a breakpoint\n      after the accumulated history, and a live run records nonzero `cache_read_tokens` attributable to\n      the message tail rather than only to the system block.\n- [ ] The Anthropic and Bedrock arms use their OWN keys (`anthropic_cache` vs\n      `bedrock_cache_messages`); a test pins that the Bedrock arm never receives a top-level\n      `cache_control`, since Bedrock rejects it outright.\n- [ ] SINGLE-TURN paths are unchanged, proven by a captured request diff that is byte-identical before\n      and after — this is the regression this change could plausibly cause.\n- [ ] The cost effect is MEASURED on a real multi-turn agentic run, before and after, and recorded.\n      A narrowly-scoped live run is sufficient and is preferred over any eval sweep.\n- [ ] make lint and make typecheck pass by exit code; the default selection is green; the Config-read\n      and env-vars drift gates both pass.","id":"dd27-0781-c8be-4e26","parent_id":"061c-ecd1-8967-4a76","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Agentic message tail is re-sent uncached every turn: O(N^2) input cost, invisible to our telemetry"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785731209645736001,"uuid":"12f55593-e3e8-425d-9227-50c124289f59"}